      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/019a969103cb8aca2da4e752240079e90bc1d19e47bdadedfb0a447a3a100367.png)\n\nThe figure above shows part of the graph of $y=f(x)$ which is defined on the interval $x\\in [-4,4].$ Given that $f(x)$ is even, which of the following gives the complete graph of $y=f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the graph of an even function must be symmetric about the $y$-axis.\n\nSo, we can obtain the missing part of the graph by reflecting the given part over the $y$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the complete graph of the function is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/dcb80b98841bd0c5f08b5ebc8f15abae62dfbe9a4ba0f3a922ea3e482318a96a.png)",
